    "notes": {
        "4941a94c-6b2c-4ace-adab-b2b0704b50e5": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 560,
            "width": 736,
            "height": 288,
            "content": "## Test data assumption: one real Nuki device\n\nNuki has no sandbox. The connected account (API token with the scopes smartlock.readOnly, smartlock.action, smartlock.auth and smartlock.log) must hold at least one Smart Lock that is online. The flow takes the first device Find Smartlocks returns, so no device ID is hardcoded.\n\n**The flow physically unlocks the device and locks it again two minutes later.** Run it only on a test lock, not on a door somebody depends on.\n\nThe trigger polls and records the state of the devices on its first check, so the first command is sent after a 2-minute Wait. Do not remove the Waits: the second one lets a check see the unlocked state before the device is locked again. Whatever state the device starts in, one of the two commands changes it."
        }
    }
